nterrupter (A) comprises a case (3) provided with a pair of projections (35) to prevent a source of light (1) and a photodetector (2) from leaving a pair of compartments (30). The projections (35) occupy areas beyond and in line with optical slits (34) formed in a first wall (32A) that defines the compartments (30) of the case (3). Since no big slits other than slits (34) are thus required in the case (3), ambient light is prevented from entering the compartments (30).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un photo-interrupteur (a) de lumière comprenant un boîtier (3) muni de deux saillies (35) retenant une source (1) lumineuse et un photodétecteur (2) dans leurs deux compartiments (30) respectifs. Ces saillies (35) occupent des zones situées au delà et dans le prolongement de deux fentes (34) optiques formées dans une première paroi (32A) délimitant les compartiments (30) du boîtier (3). Ce dispositif ne nécessitant aucune grande fente en plus de ces deux fentes (34), la lumière ambiante est empêchée pénétrer dans les compartiments (30).</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>